  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(x)=\\int_1^x \\frac{\\log t}{1+t} d t$\n$F(e)=f(e)+f\\left(\\frac{1}{e}\\right)$\n$F(e)=\\int_1^e \\frac{\\log t}{1+t} d t+\\int_1^{1 / e} \\frac{\\log t}{1+t} d t$\n$=\\int_1^e \\frac{\\log t}{1+t}+\\int_1^e \\frac{\\log t}{t(1+t)} d t$\n$=\\int_1^e \\frac{\\log t}{t} d t=\\frac{1}{2}$.",
    "image": null
  },
